<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;Make syntax isnt portable.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I don't buy this argument. About 88% of the currently over 39k distributions in my (up-to-date) [mod://CPAN::Mini] contain a &lt;c&gt;Makefile.PL&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;Update:&lt;/i&gt; To clarify: I'm not saying Makefiles are necessarily portable. The point is the solutions to the OP &lt;i&gt;can&lt;/i&gt; be implemented in a portable way, but the way the above statement is worded makes it seem like they can't. That's the problem with a four-word post; perhaps clarification would have been useful.&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
